    "result_text": "All 285 tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS). The stack-trace line in `UserRestControllerV1Tests` is just a logged expected exception from a test that passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `namesakeCount` on owner creation \u2014 the count of other owners sharing the same last name at that moment.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 added `owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner))` in the new-owner branch, alongside the existing creation-time fields. The new `countNamesakes` helper counts existing owners with a matching last name (case-insensitive, consistent with how the codebase handles city matching); the not-yet-persisted owner is naturally excluded.\n\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added the `namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter, following the `membershipNumber`/`customerCode`/`membershipTier` pattern so the value persists and is returned on later GETs.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto`; MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n4. **Schema files** \u2014 added `namesake_count` column to all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\n5. **hsqldb `data.sql`** \u2014 the seed uses positional `INSERT`s, so I appended the value (0 for all, 1 for Harold Davis who had one existing Davis at creation). h2/postgres seeds use column-list inserts of base fields only, so they needed no change.\n\nThe cp16 test verifies the first owner with a surname gets 0 and the second gets 1 \u2014 both pass.",
